In article <410@iconsys.UUCP> mmm@iconsys.UUCP (Mark Muhlestein) writes:

> I agree with the poster.  NH3.0 is too hard.  Where's the fun in
> getting killed suddenly and without any chance to do anything
> about it?

  [ ... ]

> I have almost sworn off nethack several times after being pissed off by
> once again getting killed arbitrarily on a good game.

No, you don't get killed arbitrarily in NetHack 3.0.

In NetHack 2.3 you could build an invulnerable character easely, just to
find yourself getting killed by a black dragon, for which no defence
existed.

In NetHack 3.0 it is next to impossible to build such a character, but
I have yet to find any attack for which no defence exist. You can
still be unlucky and e.g. be hit by deadly poison before you find
anything to give you poison resistance, but most often you get killed
in a fair fight, which is how it should be. You will learn how to
fight the monsters successfully. Did you *really* walked straight into
a room full of Uruk-Hai's? Why?

NetHack 3.0 depend on skill (and some luck), where 2.3 only depend on
luck. 

> I keep coming back because it *is* a good game!
>
> Any ideas on ways to decrease the frustration level?

It is good *because* it is frustrating. Otherwise, it would only be
boring (just try to play in explore or debug mode...)

No, I have not won 3.0. But I have won in the earlier versions several
times, and I have much more fun now trying to reach level 10 alive,
than I had trying to escape with the maximal number of diamonds and
gold pieces in 2.3.

If many people feel different, then maybe the HARD compile option
should be extended to include such thing as Hit/Damage for monsters
and players?


